{"id":"eber","name":"Eber","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:eber"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Eber","text":"Beyond. (1.). The third post-duluvian patriach after Shem (Gen. 10:24; 11:14). He is regarded as the founder of the Hebrew race (10:21; Num. 24:24). In Luke 3:35 he is called Heber. (2.) One of the seven heads of the families of the Gadites (1 Chr. 5:13). (3.) The oldest of the three sons of Elpaal the Benjamite (8:12). (4.) One of the heads of the familes of Benjamites in Jerusalem (22). (5.) The head of the priestly family of Amok in the time of Zerubbabel (Neh. 12:20)."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H5677","lemma":"עֵבֵר","xlit":"ʻÊbêr","gloss":"Eber, the name of two patriarchs and four Israelites","kjv":"Eber, Heber","count":11,"share":0.79},{"strong":"H6389","lemma":"פֶּלֶג","xlit":"Peleg","gloss":"Peleg, a son of Shem","kjv":"Peleg","count":3,"share":0.21},{"strong":"H3205","lemma":"יָלַד","xlit":"yâlad","gloss":"to bear young","kjv":"bear, beget, birth, born","count":5,"share":0.36},{"strong":"H6385","lemma":"פָּלַג","xlit":"pâlag","gloss":"to split","kjv":"divide","count":2,"share":0.14},{"strong":"H3355","lemma":"יׇקְטָן","xlit":"Yoqṭân","gloss":"Joktan, an Arabian patriarch","kjv":"Joktan","count":2,"share":0.14},{"strong":"H7974","lemma":"שֶׁלַח","xlit":"Shelach","gloss":"Shelach, a postdiluvian patriarch","kjv":"Salah, Shelah","count":2,"share":0.14}],"verses":["Gen.10.21","Gen.10.24","Gen.10.25","Gen.11.14","Num.24.24","1Chr.1.19","1Chr.1.25","1Chr.5.13","1Chr.8.12","1Chr.8.22","Neh.12.20","Gen.10.22","Gen.10.23","Luke.3.35"],"related":[{"id":"peleg","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.167,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"salah","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.158,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"heber","type":"cooccur","shared":3,"jaccard":0.125,"why":"3 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"shem","type":"cooccur","shared":8,"jaccard":0.092,"why":"8 verses are ind